      "math_academy_id": "q-25591",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Which of the following number lines represents the values of $x$ that satisfy $7x+5>47$ or $3x-3\\le 30?$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by solving $7x+5>47:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+5 & >47 \\\\ 7x & >47-5 \\\\ 7x & >42 \\\\ x & >\\frac{42}{7} \\\\ x & >6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/b2b7aad327466abf2472e9058317e8f5521eba35a944482e2cc3cc12cf51095b.png)\n\nThen, we solve $3x-3\\le 30:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-3 & \\le 30 \\\\ 3x & \\le 30+3 \\\\ 3x & \\le 33 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{33}{3} \\\\ x & \\le 11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/312b09109c1cb34d5820616c9aca887c6e48507be2c5045b128f9fa8c4cb0791.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14196049/assets/6681d256a848077367d83e215b4cb45edea86c49929c9c85c2aa32d8caaa2de7.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $-\\infty <x<\\infty .$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
